# Root-lane counts for `-p delphi-runtime --tests`, ALL 17 targets under sudo.
#
# LANE RUN 14 — THE FULL-HYGIENE RUN, INCLUDING A FRESHNESS CHECK THAT ACTUALLY CHECKS.
# **This closes D0A-R24-01**, which R25-05 had reopened. Measured 2026-09-06 at `af6dde0`.
#
#   EXECUTED 187 / SKIPPED 5 / reported 192     extractor rc=0
#   producers: 17/17 exited 0                   failures: 0
#   predicted 187/5/192 at af6dde0, committed ALONE and BEFORE the run — and MATCHED EXACTLY
#
# EVERY HYGIENE CHECK, CAPTURED SEPARATELY, WITH THE EVIDENCE THAT DECIDES IT. Capturing each
# check separately is not sufficient on its own — R25-05 is the case where a check WAS
# captured separately and its output still could not decide the thing it was captured for. So
# each line below names what was actually compared, not that a step ran:
#
#   account          delphi-tool:x:997:972       (gid 972, not 997 — D0A-R17-02)
#   helper digest    aba0f0ea14b751aa…           INSTALLED == STAGED, both printed
#   bwrap            0.11.1
#   free space       /run 1483M, target 4467M, /tmp 3710M — all above floor
#   forced freshness MEASURED THIS TIME. `sha256sum` over the ENUMERATED set before and after
#                    `touch runtime/src/execute.rs` + rebuild: before=17 after=17 lines, and
#                    `diff` returned EMPTY. Both counts are printed because a short list on
#                    either side is a false green, and the count is what distinguishes "all
#                    17 identical" from "the three I happened to look at". Run 13's line said
#                    "identical executable set" on the strength of `| tail -3`, which prints
#                    PATHS and never hashes anything (D0A-R25-05).
#   PAM before       439c1d1521d86e4eb011a927aff659db
#   PAM after        md5sum -c → OK              (class 16, the defect already paid for)
#   stale sessions   none, checked before AND after
#
# THE FIVE SKIPS, each quoting its own blocker from the log — a skip proves nothing, so the
# list is read rather than the count:
#   b1_daemon_binary_runs_the_assembled_flow          needs --features insecure-test-seams
#   an_unreadable_login_defs_refuses_…                this uid can read a 0000 file
#   pidfd_refuses_a_recycled_pid_barrier              user namespaces unavailable here
#   live_logind_query_path_works_or_documents_…       standing DEFER (no logind session)
#   a_regular_login_user_is_not_refused_…             running as root
#
# THREE OF THE FIVE SKIP *BECAUSE* THE RUN IS PRIVILEGED and execute unprivileged. So root's
# 187 and the unprivileged 167 are OVERLAPPING SETS, neither containing the other, and
# "187 > 167" is not a coverage claim in either direction. The memberships are read from the
# two skip LISTS; they are never computed from the two totals.
#
# BOTH LANES REPORT 192, which is the consistency check the expectation committed in advance:
# same test set, different skip distribution. A reported total other than 192 would have meant
# the SET changed — a different defect from a count mismatch.
#
# ORDERING IS CONVENTION (D0A-R22-01, still reopened). `git log` on this file and on
# `.expected` is the only evidence the prediction preceded the measurement, and it is evidence
# only because af6dde0 contains that file alone. Nothing enforces it. This is the SECOND
# consecutive run to hold under convention; that makes the failure non-guaranteed, not the
# convention sufficient.
#
# SUPERSEDED — LANE RUN 13 (`EXECUTED 177 / SKIPPED 5 / reported 182`, at 40d7fb7). Its
# counts, producer statuses, PAM integrity, stale-session sweep, helper digest, account, bwrap
# and free space were genuinely measured and are not in doubt. Its FRESHNESS line was
# withdrawn by D0A-R25-05 — the commands behind it computed no hashes — so "those binaries
# were that code" was never established for run 13 and cannot be after the fact. Run 14
# re-establishes it on the current tree rather than repairing run 13, which is why run 13 is
# superseded rather than corrected. Runs 11 and 12 were superseded by run 13 before that:
# run 11 carried hygiene, run 12 counts-and-ordering, and neither alone was the lane record.
EXECUTED=187
SKIPPED=5
